 outlet.","parent":{"$ref":"#/tables/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":539.5854525786743,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":72.0,"r":540.0054323200004,"t":564.4794016},"charspan":[0,110],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/2","text":"Table 1: Physical parameters and numerical values of the three-element Windkessel parameters for every outlet."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"a semi-implicit 3D-0D coupling scheme as seen in [9]. The full algorithm is detailed in the appendix.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":496.11545257867425,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":72.0,"r":539.9958681600002,"t":521.0094015999999},"charspan":[0,101],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/3","text":"a semi-implicit 3D-0D coupling scheme as seen in [9]. The full algorithm is detailed in the appendix."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"3.1.2 Synthetic measurements","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":465.2864267481267,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":72.0,"r":256.3073408,"t":475.7802671999999},"charspan":[0,28],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/4","text":"3.1.2 Synthetic measurements"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The forward solution is generated with a time step of dt = 1 ms and undersampled in time to dt meas = 15 ms , leading to a total of 56 measurements. From the solution of the forward problem, we simulate a PC-MRI acquisition by subsampling into a rectangular measurement mesh with a resolution of [2 mm, 2 mm, 2 mm ] and then applying the process described in Section 2.1 with a venc of double the maximal velocity. The magnitude is modelled as","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":385.34645257867413,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":72.0,"r":540.00578432,"t":453.5784015999999},"charspan":[0,443],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/5","text":"The forward solution is generated with a time step of dt = 1 ms and undersampled in time to dt meas = 15 ms , leading to a total of 56 measurements. From the solution of the forward problem, we simulate a PC-MRI acquisition by subsampling into a rectangular measurement mesh with a resolution of [2 mm, 2 mm, 2 mm ] and then applying the process described in Section 2.1 with a venc of double the maximal velocity. The magnitude is modelled as"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"M ( x ) = { 1 . 0 if x is in the lumen of the vessel 0 . 5 otherwise. (16)","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":342.41545257867415,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":179.925,"r":540.0006121600002,"t":374.7652079999998},"charspan":[0,74],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/6","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Finally a complex Gaussian noise ϵ ∈ C N is added with a signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) of 15. Fifty independent realizations of the noise were generated.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":301.84745257867417,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":72.00000000000003,"r":540.0030662400001,"t":328.35757829999983},"charspan":[0,151],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/7","text":"Finally a complex Gaussian noise ϵ ∈ C N is added with a signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) of 15. Fifty independent realizations of the noise were generated."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"For comparison, we reconstructed velocity measurements from these synthetic measurements using the Berkeley Advanced Reconstruction Toolbox (BART)[11]. BART is a command-line-based software that provides a flexible framework of compressed sensing methods, as well as tools for simulation, pre-processing, and image reconstruction, providing a multitude of different regularization options. In this work, we have used this toolbox for compressed sensing reconstructions of the velocities, using total variation in time as for the regularization.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":200.72645257867407,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":72.00000000000003,"r":540.0054323200001,"t":297.8494015999998},"charspan":[0,544],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/8","text":"For comparison, we reconstructed velocity measurements from these synthetic measurements using the Berkeley Advanced Reconstruction Toolbox (BART)[11]. BART is a command-line-based software that provides a flexible framework of compressed sensing methods, as well as tools for simulation, pre-processing, and image reconstruction, providing a multitude of different regularization options. In this work, we have used this toolbox for compressed sensing reconstructions of the velocities, using total variation in time as for the regularization."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Next, the sampling mask is applied to these simulated frequency space measurements. We take a 2D subsampled mask in the x -y -plane and sample fully in the z -direction as in [4]. We consider different subsampling rates R = N sampled N total = 8 , 16 , 32, with two different masks: the pseudo-spiral mask and the pseudo-random Gaussian mask, which is sampled according to a Gaussian probability distribution, as shown in Figure 2. For the pseudo-spiral mask, the points are placed evenly on a cartesian grid along a spiral with six turns and a final radius reaching the edge of the mask.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":99.60545257867432,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":72.0,"r":540.0042368000003,"t":196.72840159999976},"charspan":[0,588],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/9","text":"Next, the sampling mask is applied to these simulated frequency space measurements. We take a 2D subsampled mask in the x -y -plane and sample fully in the z -direction as in [4]. We consider different subsampling rates R = N sampled N total = 8 , 16 , 32, with two different masks: the pseudo-spiral mask and the pseudo-random Gaussian mask, which is sampled according to a Gaussian probability distribution, as shown in Figure 2. For the pseudo-spiral mask, the points are placed evenly on a cartesian grid along a spiral with six turns and a final radius reaching the edge of the mask."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","label":"page_footer","orig":"10","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":69.7174525786744,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":300.147,"r":311.85353184,"t":80.1654016},"charspan":[0,2],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/10","text":"10"}],"version":"1.10.0"}